      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s20w",
          "text": "Airbag deployment does not automatically mean your car is totaled, despite how serious the crash feels.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b20z",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s20y",
          "text": "Insurance companies compare repair costs against your vehicle’s market value before deciding whether it’s totaled.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b211",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s210",
          "text": "Colorado law defines a total loss when repair costs exceed the car’s fair market value before damage.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b213",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s212",
          "text": "Airbag deployment significantly increases repair costs, often pushing vehicles closer to a total-loss decision.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b215",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s214",
          "text": "Disputes with insurers over valuation and payouts are common, especially when total-loss determinations are involved.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b219",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l216",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/car-accident-statistics-in-denver-colorado-2025/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s217",
          "text": "Accidents across Denver",
          "marks": [
            "l216"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s218",
          "text": " often leave drivers looking at a damaged vehicle and trying to make sense of what just happened, especially when airbags deploy, and the crash feels more severe than expected. At that moment, it is completely normal to feel overwhelmed, unsure about your car’s condition, and worried about what comes next.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b21i",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l21d",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/denver-car-accident-lawyer/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21a",
          "text": "Many drivers search ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21b",
          "text": "“If your airbags deploy, is your car totaled?”",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21c",
          "text": " because it creates uncertainty about both safety and financial impact. The ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21e",
          "text": "car accident attorneys",
          "marks": [
            "l21d"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21f",
          "text": " at ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21g",
          "text": "Dormer Harpring",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21h",
          "text": " have seen how quickly that uncertainty can turn into frustration once insurance companies step in and start making decisions.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b21k",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21j",
          "text": "In Denver, when airbags deploy, it usually indicates a forceful collision, often at higher speeds, which can help demonstrate how serious the crash was. While airbags are designed to limit more severe injuries, their deployment can still lead to issues such as burns or fractures, and the cost of replacing the system can significantly increase the risk of a total loss.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b21m",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21l",
          "text": "Understanding Car Total Loss Criteria",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b21t",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l21q",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://dmv.colorado.gov/salvage-vehicles"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21n",
          "text": "A clear answer to ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21o",
          "text": "“If your airbags deploy, is your car totaled?”",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21p",
          "text": " begins with how Colorado defines a total loss, which centers on the financial balance between repair costs and vehicle value rather than the airbags alone. According to the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21r",
          "text": "Colorado Department of Motor Vehicles",
          "marks": [
            "l21q"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21s",
          "text": ", a vehicle qualifies as salvage when repair costs exceed its fair market value before the crash under C.R.S. 42-6-102(17)(a)(I). That definition places the decision in the hands of insurers and valuation methods rather than a single mechanical event.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b21v",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21u",
          "text": "Insurance companies rely on actual cash value (ACV) to determine whether repairs make sense, and once repair estimates approach or exceed that number, a total loss designation becomes more likely. Airbags play a role because replacement costs rise quickly, though the core decision always comes back to value versus repair expense.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b21x",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21w",
          "text": "When Is a Car Considered Totaled?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b21z",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s21y",
          "text": "A car is considered totaled when repair costs exceed its pre-accident value; while that definition sounds simple, real claims rarely unfold that way because multiple variables shape both value and repair costs.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b221",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s220",
          "text": "Vehicle age, mileage, condition before the crash, and current demand influence valuation, while labor rates and parts availability drive repair estimates. In many cases, insurers apply internal thresholds, typically between 50% and 75% of a vehicle’s value, though those percentages vary by company and policy.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b223",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s222",
          "text": "A newer vehicle with moderate damage may remain repairable even after airbag deployment, especially if structural components remain intact. By contrast, an older vehicle with lower market value may reach total loss status after relatively limited repairs. That contrast explains why two similar crashes can lead to very different outcomes.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b22l",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s224",
          "text": "Drivers often expect a clear yes-or-no answer to ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s225",
          "text": "“If",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s226",
          "text": " ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s227",
          "text": "your",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s228",
          "text": " ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s229",
          "text": "airbags",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22a",
          "text": " ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22b",
          "text": "deploy,",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22c",
          "text": " ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22d",
          "text": "is",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22e",
          "text": " ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22f",
          "text": "your",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22g",
          "text": " ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22h",
          "text": "car",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22i",
          "text": " ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22j",
          "text": "totaled?”",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22k",
          "text": " However, insurers evaluate the full scope of damage and financial feasibility before reaching a decision, which is why understanding how these thresholds apply can make the process feel less unpredictable.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b22n",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22m",
          "text": "What Does Airbag Deployment Have to Do With a Car Being Totaled?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b22p",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22o",
          "text": "Airbag deployment increases the likelihood of a total loss by significantly raising repair costs. Modern airbag systems include sensors, control modules, and multiple integrated components that require replacement after deployment.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b22u",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l22r",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.nhtsa.gov/vehicle-safety/air-bags"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22q",
          "text": "As the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22s",
          "text": "National Highway Traffic Safety Administration",
          "marks": [
            "l22r"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22t",
          "text": " notes, a signal from the vehicle’s control unit triggers a rapid chemical reaction that inflates the airbag in a fraction of a second, which explains both its effectiveness and the potential for injury during deployment. Even one deployed airbag can add substantial cost when labor and calibration are factored in.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b22w",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22v",
          "text": "When repair costs increase, especially when multiple airbags deploy or structural damage accompanies the crash, the gap between repair costs and vehicle value narrows quickly. Hidden damage also plays a role, since impacts strong enough to trigger airbags often affect internal systems and structural components not immediately visible.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b22y",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s22x",
          "text": "This explains why many drivers question whether a vehicle becomes totaled after airbags deploy, even though airbags do not determine the outcome on their own.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "image",
      "_key": "i22z",
